  "conclusion": "C2 result: 3-4 trim bits on the EXISTING per-column write-DAC restore the per-column offset from the fatal regime back to within the 0.15 pp MNIST noise floor (e.g. sigma_col=8 popcount: untrimmed 96.35% -> b=3 96.82% ~ baseline 97.00%). Cost is near-free: the trim is a STATIC per-column code (set once at calibration, amortized over all writes) and the write path already dominates energy (~98.7%); the extra DAC switching is <1% of the ~1.61 pJ end-to-end write. => quantifies the thesis's 'DAC calibration + drift compensation' as a concrete near-free mechanism, and pairs with C1 (slope-matched SA) as the Hero's calibration half. Closes errata R4's calibration side."
